# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/deploy/env.catalog — every .env variable the stack needs.
# Read by scripts/deploy/lib/manager.sh to prompt for, generate, validate and
# report on the manager's .env. One variable per line:
#
#   NAME|REQUIRED|KIND|GENERATOR|VALIDATOR|DEFAULT|DESCRIPTION
#
#   REQUIRED   required | optional   (required = docker-stack.yml has no default)
#   KIND       secret | plain        (secrets: hidden input, masked everywhere)
#   GENERATOR  none | base64:N | hex:N   (`g` at the prompt generates one)
#   VALIDATOR  - | nonempty | b64len32 | minlen8 | minlen16 | minlen32 | https_url
#              | domain | email | int | number | bool | mem_size | bucket | ident | dbname | tz | hostport
#   DEFAULT    - | fixed:VALUE | default:VALUE | domain:TEMPLATE ({D} = the domain)
#
# NEVER change these after first deploy (data becomes unreadable / keys stop
# working): KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY, SFS_API_KEY_PEPPER, POSTGRES_*, MINIO_ROOT_*.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_APP_USER|required|plain|none|dbname|default:apollo|App database user (only applied when the database is first created)
POSTGRES_APP_PASSWORD|required|secret|hex:24|minlen8|-|App database password (only applied when the database is first created)
POSTGRES_APP_DB|required|plain|none|dbname|default:apollo_sfs|App database name
POSTGRES_KC_USER|required|plain|none|dbname|default:keycloak|Keycloak database user
POSTGRES_KC_PASSWORD|required|secret|hex:24|minlen8|-|Keycloak database password
POSTGRES_KC_DB|required|plain|none|dbname|default:keycloak|Keycloak database name
KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY|required|secret|base64:32|b64len32|-|Master key wrapping every user's file key (base64 of exactly 32 bytes) — NEVER change once files exist
SESSION_KEY|required|secret|base64:48|minlen16|-|Session cookie signing key
MINIO_ROOT_USER|required|plain|none|nonempty|default:apollo-minio|MinIO root user, shared by every MinIO instance
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD|required|secret|hex:24|minlen8|-|MinIO root password (at least 8 characters)
MINIO_BUCKET_NAME|required|plain|none|bucket|default:apollo-sfs|Primary storage bucket on every MinIO instance
KEYCLOAK_REALM|required|plain|none|nonempty|fixed:apollo-sfs-realm|Keycloak realm (must match keycloak/import/realm.json)
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID|required|plain|none|nonempty|fixed:apollo-sfs-api|Confidential Keycloak client the API uses
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET|required|secret|hex:32|minlen16|-|That client's secret — deploy.sh sets it in Keycloak after a fresh realm import
KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL|required|plain|none|https_url|domain:https://auth.{D}|Keycloak's browser-facing origin
KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_HOST|required|plain|none|domain|domain:auth.{D}|Keycloak hostname kept pointed here by the DDNS service
KEYCLOAK_ADMIN|required|plain|none|nonempty|default:admin|Bootstrap Keycloak admin (used only on an empty Keycloak database)
KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD|required|secret|hex:16|minlen8|-|Bootstrap Keycloak admin password
COOKIE_DOMAIN|required|plain|none|domain|domain:{D}|Cookie domain (bare domain)
APP_BASE_URL|required|plain|none|https_url|domain:https://{D}|The app's public URL
MAIL_FROM|required|plain|none|email|domain:noreply@{D}|Sender address for app mail
MAIL_DOMAIN|required|plain|none|domain|domain:{D}|Mail domain (Postfix allowed sender + hostname)
CLOUDFLARE_TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY|required|secret|none|nonempty|-|Turnstile secret key (Cloudflare dashboard)
CLOUDFLARE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY|required|plain|none|nonempty|-|Turnstile site key (Cloudflare dashboard)
SFS_API_KEY_PEPPER|required|secret|base64:48|minlen32|-|Pepper for SFS API key hashes (at least 32 bytes) — NEVER rotate
SENDGRID_SMTP_PASSWORD|required|secret|none|nonempty|-|SendGrid API key with Mail Send permission (Postfix relay)
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN|required|secret|none|nonempty|-|Cloudflare API token limited to DNS edit (DDNS)
CLOUDFLARE_RECORD_NAME|required|plain|none|domain|domain:{D}|DNS record the DDNS service keeps pointed here
NODE_AGENT_TOKEN|required|secret|hex:32|minlen16|-|Shared secret for node-agent → node-metrics-ingest pushes
RECOGNITION_TOKEN|optional|secret|hex:32|-|-|Shared secret for api → recognition sidecar (empty disables AI recognition)
COOKIE_SECURE|optional|plain|none|bool|default:true|Secure cookies (only the exact string true enables them)
SENDGRID_WEBHOOK_SECRET|optional|secret|hex:24|-|-|Token in SendGrid's inbound-parse URL (?token=…)
QUOTA_WARNING_THRESHOLD_PERCENT|optional|plain|none|int|default:80|Quota warning e-mail threshold (%)
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|PayPal live client id (payments)
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET|optional|secret|none|-|-|PayPal live client secret
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|PayPal live webhook id
PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|PayPal sandbox client id (admin sandbox toggle)
PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET|optional|secret|none|-|-|PayPal sandbox client secret
PAYPAL_SANDBOX_WEBHOOK_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|PayPal sandbox webhook id
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|Google OAuth web client id (social login)
GOOGLE_WEB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET|optional|secret|none|-|-|Google OAuth web client secret
PREMIUM_TIER_PRICE_CENTS|optional|plain|none|int|default:999|Premium price in cents
PREMIUM_TIER_CURRENCY|optional|plain|none|-|default:USD|Premium price currency
TZ|optional|plain|none|tz|default:UTC|IANA time zone for the api (the 4am reconciliation)
RECOGNITION_CPU_LIMIT|optional|plain|none|number|default:6|CPU limit for the recognition sidecar (~50% of the manager)
RECOGNITION_MEM_LIMIT|optional|plain|none|mem_size|default:16G|Memory limit for the recognition sidecar (needs a unit, e.g. 16G)
VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID|optional|plain|none|-|-|Azure AD client id baked into the frontend image (email backup Microsoft sign-in)
REGISTRY|optional|plain|none|hostport|-|Image registry HOST:PORT (kept in sync by deploy.sh)
